        "columns": [
          {
            "text": [
              {
                "type": "heading",
                "level": 2,
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "How can the investments that Sidney Cano proposes us to transform the role of the economy in the regeneration of our territories?",
                    "type": "text"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "",
                    "type": "text"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "Laura Comas, member of Resilience.Earth, guides this conversation where we enter into the experience and vision of Sidney Cano, co-founder of the ",
                    "type": "text"
                  },
                  {
                    "url": "https://www.duitglobal.com/",
                    "type": "link",
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "text": "Duit Group",
                        "type": "text"
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "a pioneering initiative in the area of transformative investment and the creation of development communities for the regeneration of local economies. Cano invites us to rethink the way we understand investment, emphasizing the social, environmental and community value of each project. ",
                    "type": "text"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "Through its trajectory, we discover how regenerative economies can become a real and sustainable alternative within the current economic system. With emphasis on collaboration, care and structural transformation, Sidney Cano shares concrete examples of processes that drive change from below, connecting companies, people and territories.",
                    "type": "text"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "This interview is an invitation to reflect on how we can invest in regenerating, and on the role that each of us can play in building a living, resilient and rooted economic future in the common good.",
                    "type": "text"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "",
                    "type": "text"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ],
