          {
            "text": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "The conversation with Sidney Cano reminds us that the economy can be much more than a tool of production or performance: it can become a living fabric of relationships that connects people, territories and shared values. His words invite us to imagine a new way of investing - one that puts life in the center, that takes care of processes and that commits itself to regeneration as a principle of abundance.",
                    "type": "text"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "Through the eyes of Laura Comas, this conversation becomes a space of facilitation and listening, where questions arise that challenge us as a cooperative society and as individuals: what does it really mean to generate value? How can we grow projects that feed the common?",
                    "type": "text"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "children": [
                  {
                    "bold": true,
                    "text": "The dialogue between Sidney and Laura leaves us with certainty: regeneration is possible when the economy is put in the service of life, and when creativity and cooperation become the true engines of a transformation.",
                    "type": "text"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ],
